    <string name="changelog_text_v1_1_5">What\'s new in version 1.1.5:\n* **Bug fixes:** Fixed a compatibility issue that caused the app to crash on Android 14 and older devices when viewing notifications.</string>
    <string name="changelog_text_v1_1_6">WHAT\'S NEW\n• Reading Progress: The current reading progress is now displayed directly on the book\'s details page.\n• Production Readiness: Internal adjustments and final configuration for the official launch of the application on the Google Play Store.\n\nFIXES\n• Fixed the bug that prevented reading progress from updating correctly (resolved technical issue with CSRF Referer).\n\nSpecial thanks to @HBB for their contribution to this update!</string>
    <string name="changelog_text_v1_1_7">WHAT\'S NEW\n• Danish Language: Added support for Danish.\n• Translation Improvements: Extracted hardcoded Spanish texts and completed missing translations across all languages.\n\nFIXES\n• Search State: Preserved the search state when rotating the screen.\n• ISBN Detection: Refactored and improved ISBN detection logic.\n• Login/OkHttp: Unified the User-Agent between OkHttp and the login WebView.\n• Scraper Markers: Removed hardcoded Spanish markers from the scraper.\n\nSpecial thanks to @HBB for all their incredible contributions to this release!</string>
    <string name="changelog_text_v1_1_8">WHAT\'S NEW\n• Finish reading: You can now mark a book as finished directly from its details or your profile. This action will close the reading session and add the book to your reading goal (just like on the Bookwyrm website).</string>
    <string name="changelog_text_v1_1_9">WHAT\'S NEW\n• Book detail page: The book detail view is now a full-screen page with tabs (Summary, Reviews, and Details) instead of a pop-up dialog. The back button returns to the previous list without losing your scroll position.\n• Enhanced shelves: Book cards now show author, user rating (with half stars), number of pages, language (as a flag), and reading dates. Data is fetched once and cached locally.\n• Shelf sorting: You can now sort your shelves by title (A–Z / Z–A), by finish date (newest/oldest), and by rating (highest/lowest).\n\nFIXES\n• Scraping: Fixed three bugs that prevented fetching quotes, updating reading progress, and displaying some book covers.\n• Shelf display: Fixed a bug that caused duplicate books when sorting or paginating shelves.\n• Translations: Completed all missing translations across the 16 supported languages.\n\nSpecial thanks to @HBB for their outstanding contributions to this release!</string>
    <string name="changelog_text_v1_2_0">WHAT\'S NEW\n• Customizable profile: You can now reorder and hide the different sections of your profile to your liking. The order is saved on the device and changes are applied only when you press \"Save\".\n• Reading statistics: Added a new card on the profile with charts and key figures: total books read and this year, accumulated pages, and a bar chart with the history of books per year.\n• Reading pace: The annual challenge card now indicates if you are ahead or behind your goal based on the current day. It also shows your average days taken to read a book (this year and in total).\n• New charts on the profile: Most read authors, ratings breakdown, and languages and formats of the books you read (automatically detected from shelves).\n• \"To Read\" shelf: Added a quick access row on the profile with the covers of the books from your \"To Read\" shelf.\n• Translations completed: Translated all profile strings (including plural rules) to the 17 languages supported by the application.\n\nFIXES AND INTERNAL IMPROVEMENTS\n• Notifications: Fixed a silent error (403 CSRF) that prevented the \"Clear all notifications\" button from actually working on the server. An error message is now displayed if the operation fails.\n• Shelves cache: Fixed an issue where only the first page of the shelf was saved when using the app offline. Now the entire shelf is cached when scrolling through it.\n• Shared stars: The rating stars component (RatingStars) has been refactored to reuse it throughout the app consistently, and the obsolete half-star icon has been replaced with its correct version for RTL reading.</string>
